The skips are quarantined known bugs, shapes the library declines,
Stream-K cases that need `TENSILE_SOLUTION_SELECTION_METHOD=2`, and on
the shared MI210, cases that need more free memory than it had.

Earlier development runs, on gfx942 (MI300A):

- Self-tests: each of six deliberate source mutations, four in the host
code and two in the GPU kernels, made at least one self-test fail.
- With the ROCM-31016 fix reverted, 170 of the 1,093 solutions failed.
The first reported 1793 elements never written, starting at element
offset 2147481599, which is the 2^32-byte boundary for bf16. With the
fix in place, all 1,093 passed in 144 s.
- With the fix reverted, each failure names the kernel, for example
`Cijk_Ailk_Bljk_BBS_BH_Bias_HA_S_SAV_UserArgs_MT128x448x32_…` (library
index 75677). The placement record shows C and D, each about 4 GiB,
crossing a 4 GiB boundary.
- Same shapes, `unit_check` before and fast_check after: ldd = 1049100
f32 went from 14.4 s to 0.7 s, and lda = 1049100 f32 from 8.3 s to 1.2
s.
- `standard` tier (smoke, quick, pre_checkin), run with the stack's
second PR: 71,379 run, one failure, `matmul_fallback_compute_fp16`,
which passes at the stack tip under ROCm 10.2 on an MI300X (see #12960).

